title The anchor landed and four records stayed behind
prompt The baton -- patchouli's lane, open the round, take the next agent-doable lap reds first
think Opened cold and held still while it read. The cold endurance run named rye_struct_fields RED, and it is a Mantra structure -- mine, not a peer's.
obs THE GUARD WAS BUILT FOR EXACTLY THIS AND THE PLACARDS NEVER MOVED. rye_struct_fields_witness.rish names, in its own header, the two movements it was built to unlock -- the identity gap wanting a fourth field on Line, the diff anchor wanting one on Diff -- as waiting on a lock with no bolt in it (%500). Both landed at %689 on 20260916. Line declares text gen pos site run ord against a placard of five; Diff declares site inserts deletes replaces after against a placard of three.
obs ONE RED STOOD FOR TWO. The Diff placard sat BEHIND the Line one -- the first assert refuses and the second is never read -- so the cold pass reported a single failure over two stale records.
obs THE SAME STALENESS STOOD IN PROSE, WHERE NOTHING WAS READING. mantra/src/weave.rye's head said every insert lands at the END of the document and called the anchor a seam rather than a lap, while apply reads diff.after at line 1413 and gives the insert the anchor's ord and run. annotate's header said a line cannot land between two existing ones. Both false in a file whose own head declares so the head promises exactly what the code does.
obs THAT HEADER RECORDS THIS AS ITS SECOND SUCH STAY. It kept an elder cost claim for a day on 20260908.031547 and wrote that down inside itself, three lines above code that had already moved. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
obs THE RECORD OF A MODULE HAS MORE THAN ONE SURFACE AND THE TREE HAD LOOMED ONE. The field surface was guarded and reddened within the hour. The prose surface was guarded for the operations list alone, so a field arriving -- which is exactly when a head goes stale -- reached nothing. mantra_weave_head_scan.sh now enumerates Diff's fields and reads them against the struct both ways.
obs THE SCAN GOT THE CONTROL IT NEVER HAD. Standing since %506 with four witnesses asserting its verdict, every leg proved it passes and none proved it bites. Each refusal is now planted in a pen copy and LIFTED, so a bite is shown beside the same file answering ok.
obs A FIELD LINE AND AN OPERATION LINE DIFFER BY ONE PARENTHESIS, and that is the partition worth planting: a field line whose PROSE carries a parenthesis must still read as a field. Mutation 1 drops the guard and that leg is the only one that falls.
obs THE RESIDUE IS NAMED RATHER THAN HIDDEN. An insert that OPENS the document has a null anchor and still takes the counter's answer, so it lands at the end. The repaired head says so.
obs MY ROW PUSHED THE LEDGER OVER ITS BOUND, which is the honest cost of a long row. Regenerated the headline and folded a closed row to a shelf; equinox_e123_living_pin_guard and declared_ceiling were reading that same over-bound pin and went green with it.
obs THEN THE SEND TOOK BOTH BACK, AND THAT IS THE DERIVED SPINE WORKING. A peer published its own %766 while I worked, and folded %680 to a shelf of its own in the same window. Mine was the unshared row, so mine renumbered to %773 off the anointed spine and my duplicate fold was dropped; the stamp 20260916.082030 never moved, which is the whole point of the key being the stamp. After the peer's folds the pin reads 65,512 against 65,536 and needed no fold from me at all.
obs TWO REDS ARRIVED MID-LAP AND ARE NOT MINE. ce4166b75 landed at 07:50 between my cold and hot passes carrying 33 asserts and 2 emit sites, so rune_assert_sweep reads 6,482 against 6,480 and build_target 48 against 47. Pheromone's lane, with a live claim on it; named rather than taken.
